# Line endings.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and deployed on Linux. Git's autocrlf would
# otherwise check shell scripts out with CRLF, and Linux then rejects the
# shebang itself:
#
#     ./render-build.sh: /usr/bin/env: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# which reads as a missing interpreter rather than an invisible carriage
# return. Anything executed on the server is pinned to LF.

*           text=auto

*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.yaml      text eol=lf
*.yml       text eol=lf

# Windows-only tooling stays CRLF so it opens cleanly in Notepad and friends.
*.ps1       text eol=crlf
*.bat       text eol=crlf
*.cmd       text eol=crlf

# Binary assets — never touch these.
*.png       binary
*.jpg       binary
*.jpeg      binary
*.gif       binary
*.webp      binary
*.ico       binary
*.ttf       binary
*.otf       binary
*.woff      binary
*.woff2     binary
*.apk       binary
*.aab       binary
*.jar       binary
*.keystore  binary
*.jks       binary
